<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sun Int'l half yr shr, div edges up.</title>
<headline>Sun Int'l half yr shr, div edges up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     26.4	  vs 25.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 15.5	  vs 15.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings rising to between 26 and 29 cents per share with a consensus of 27.8. They expected a dividend of around 15.8 cents.  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	  208.8	  vs 198.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  277.3	  vs 252.9</p>
<p>    Tax			 68.5	  vs  54.2</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   11.7	  vs  21.8</p>
<p>    Turnover	     1,168.4	  vs 1,098.2</p>
<p>Div payable: March 27</p>
<p>On register: March 7</p>
<p>Full name: Sun International (South Africa) Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group expected pre-tax profits to increase in the second half of the year as a result of improved operating profits and better cash flow. An increase in the tax charge for the year would, however, impact on attributable earnings which were expected to be ahead of the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
